  "id": "COMPOUND:32420 - PROTEIN:705",
  "verbalization": "Oblonganoside C appears to have a shared target relationship with Ent-Gloeosteretriol, which in turn targets the Casein kinase II subunit alpha. This pathway is supported by three distinct but overlapping evidence chains, all of which point to Ent-Gloeosteretriol as a critical mediator in the interaction between Oblonganoside C and the Casein kinase II subunit alpha. The scores from the three paths suggest a consistent and significant relationship, though the exact nature of the interaction remains somewhat indirect. The presence of multiple targets (Serine/threonine-protein kinase ICK, NCI-H1734, and Tyrosine-protein kinase Fer) indicates that Ent-Gloeosteretriol may act as a central node in a broader signaling network, potentially influencing multiple downstream pathways. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of Ent-Gloeosteretriol in linking Oblonganoside C to the Casein kinase II subunit alpha, though further experimental validation would be needed to confirm the precise mechanism of action.",
